## CWE rule
CWE-20 — Improper Input Validation
Description: Input is not validated (type, length, range, format) before it is used, opening the way to other defects.
Vulnerability indicators:
- Fields of a packet, file or argument used directly as a length, index or offset
- Missing checks on ranges and on consistency between fields
Safe patterns:
- Explicit validation of ranges and lengths right after reading
- Parsers that reject malformed input

